``` DEPLOYABLE TEMPLATE. Splunk, JSON-sourced index. Not run in CI.
    Confirm the index, sourcetype, and field extraction against your
    deployment before use.

    Assumes emitted events (elicitation_defense_lab schema.py, or the
    equivalent JSON the static page's event view produces) are shipped to
    Splunk via HEC into index=elicitation_assessment,
    sourcetype=elicitation:assessment:json. There is no elicitation-defense-lab
    backend that does this shipping today; an org adopting this tool would
    need to stand up that pipeline first. See docs/limitations.md.

    spath pulls the fields out explicitly rather than assuming
    INDEXED_EXTRACTIONS=json is set in props.conf for the sourcetype; drop
    the spath calls if your deployment already extracts fields at index
    time.

    Same three views as detections/spl/awareness_and_reporting.spl, against
    the real ingested schema instead of the reference index name. ```

``` View 1: subjects whose self-assessment landed in the high tier. ```
index=elicitation_assessment sourcetype="elicitation:assessment:json"
| spath
| where module="self" AND tier="high"
| table _time subject_id tier overall_score class_scores

``` View 2: interaction events where the subject said they would report the contact. ```
index=elicitation_assessment sourcetype="elicitation:assessment:json"
| spath
| where module="interaction" AND reporting_flag="true"
| table _time subject_id tier overall_score class_scores

``` View 3: per-subject trend of overall_score across all modules, oldest first. ```
index=elicitation_assessment sourcetype="elicitation:assessment:json"
| spath
| where isnotnull(subject_id)
| table subject_id module _time overall_score
| sort 0 subject_id, _time
